# Orange Pi 3 Project Standards

## Scope

- Custom work lives in `meta-local/` (recipes, scripts, machine config).
- Do not edit upstream layers (`poky/`, `meta-sunxi/`, `meta-arm/`, …) unless fixing an upstream bug or the user asks.
- Image target: `core-image-khepri` for Orange Pi 3 (`orange-pi-3` machine).

## Shell Scripts

Host scripts: `meta-local/scripts/`. On-target tools: `meta-local/recipes-support/*/files/` → `/usr/sbin/*`.

```bash
#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail

die() { printf 'ERROR: %s\n' "$*" >&2; exit 1; }
log() { printf '%s\n' "$*"; }

TARGET="${TARGET:-root@192.168.3.71}"   # env overrides with sensible defaults
```

- Use `#!/bin/bash` + `pipefail` on host; `#!/bin/sh` + `set -eu` on target (BusyBox).
- Configurable behavior via env vars, not positional args (see existing scripts).
- Add a header comment and `usage()` for user-facing tools.
- Docs (user-facing READMEs):
  - Host script usage **only** in `meta-local/scripts/README.md`
  - On-target `/usr/sbin/*` usage **only** in the top-level `README.md`
  - Recipe READMEs may inventory and link, not repeat the same command blocks
- Agent rules (`.cursor/rules`): do not restate full host/on-target usage;
  point at those READMEs. May add agent-only constraints (e.g. `OUT=` under
  `build-orangepi3/tmp/`, which `SSH_BIND` to prefer).
- When changing scripts or on-target tools, update the matching README above.

## Yocto / Recipes

- Prefer `.bbappend` over copying upstream recipes.
- Install files via `SRC_URI`, `do_install`, and `FILES:${PN}` — not ad-hoc rootfs edits.
- `local.conf` must include `require conf/distro/include/orangepi3-graphics.inc`.

## Yocto build directory

- **Always** use `build-orangepi3/` only. Never `oe-init-build-env` / `bitbake` against repo-root `build/` (or any other build dir).
- Init and build:

```bash
source poky/oe-init-build-env build-orangepi3
bitbake core-image-khepri
```

- Do not create or populate a top-level `build/` directory.

## Debug screenshots / video

- Temporary host-side debug images and videos (HDMI SHM shots, camera
  frames, short clips) go under `build-orangepi3/tmp/`, not the repo
  root. See `board-debug-chat` for capture commands.

## A/B Updates & Flashing

After rebuilding the image (`bitbake core-image-khepri` in `build-orangepi3`),
flash with [`push-ab-update.sh`](meta-local/scripts/README.md) — do not
hand-roll SSH update steps and do not change that script. Prefer
`SSH_BIND=192.168.3.6` (ethernet) or `192.168.3.37` (WiFi on dual-NIC hosts).

## Host audio (tone / spectrum tests)

- Never change host audio routing or settings — not even for tests.
- Forbidden: `pactl set-default-sink`, `set-sink-mute` / `set-sink-volume` on sinks, forcing ALSA `hw:`/`plughw:` devices, WirePlumber/GNOME sound reconfiguration, or any other host audio preference change.
- Play only to the **current system default** output (`paplay` / Pulse `default` with **no** `-d` / device override; same for `ffmpeg -f pulse default`).
- If the tone is silent: report the active Default Sink / Description and stop; do **not** switch sinks to “make it work”.

## General

- Minimize diff scope; match surrounding naming and style.
- Only commit or push when the user explicitly asks.